  "articleBody": "Nothing's worse than installing a new door only to find the frame is crooked or the door doesn't close properly. It's a common frustration, and usually, it boils down to a few key framing mistakes that are easy to make if you're not super careful. One of the biggest culprits is not getting the rough opening perfectly square and plumb from the get-go. If your king studs, jack studs, or header aren't level and plumb before the door unit goes in, you'll be fighting an uphill battle. Another frequent issue is making the rough opening too tight. You need that extra space for shimming and making micro-adjustments to get the door unit just right. Forgetting to allow for the thickness of the door frame itself is another one. And, of course, if the wall you're working in isn't completely flat or plumb, it can transfer those imperfections to your door frame. If you're experiencing these issues, or if you want to avoid them in the first place, calling in a professional like HH Remodeling can save you a lot of time and frustration. We're experts in getting door frames perfectly aligned and functioning beautifully.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
